&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/allfridhosaragii/FlowGuard-AI/pull/14" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/allfridhosaragii/FlowGuard-AI/pull/14&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Independent Testing Made the Project Stronger
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Alongside TestSprite, I used GitHub Actions to run independent automated tests.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After the final pull request was merged, the project successfully completed:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;✅ &lt;strong&gt;118/118 Vitest tests passed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;✅ &lt;strong&gt;70/70 Playwright Chromium tests passed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These results provided additional evidence for the tested application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Of course, passing automated tests does not guarantee that software is completely free of bugs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But having multiple verification methods helps developers better understand which behaviors have been tested.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-merge GitHub Actions evidence:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/allfridhosaragii/FlowGuard-AI/actions/runs/40273469302" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/allfridhosaragii/FlowGuard-AI/actions/runs/40273469302&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I Loved Most About TestSprite
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After using TestSprite during Hackathon Season 4, several features stood out to me.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automated Pull Request Testing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I appreciated how TestSprite brought automated verification into the GitHub development workflow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear Test Results&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The distinction between Passed, Failed, and Blocked encouraged me to interpret testing results more carefully.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality-Focused Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The earlier blocked case encouraged investigation and improvements to keyboard accessibility.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GitHub Integration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Connecting automated testing with pull request checks made quality verification part of the development process.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Verifiable Evidence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Being able to connect test results with a specific pull request and tested commit made it easier to explain what had actually been verified.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For someone developing a reliability-focused project like FlowGuard AI, these capabilities were especially meaningful.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


My Feedback: Making TestSprite Even Better
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My experience with TestSprite throughout this hackathon was positive.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I genuinely appreciated how its automated testing workflow helped me pay more attention to verification, accessibility, and software quality.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If I could suggest one improvement, it would be &lt;strong&gt;even richer diagnostics for blocked browser tests&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Additional execution traces, screenshots, environment information, and clearer explanations of where a scenario stopped could make debugging easier.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When a browser test becomes blocked, developers sometimes need to investigate whether the issue is related to application behavior, test configuration, or the testing environment.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;More detailed diagnostic information would help developers investigate those possibilities more efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I believe this would make an already valuable testing workflow even more useful.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


More Than Just 97 Passing Tests
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Looking back on this journey, I realized that the most valuable result wasn't simply achieving a green testing dashboard.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It was the development process behind it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I built an application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I integrated automated testing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I encountered a blocked test.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I investigated the application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I made improvements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And I continued verifying the results.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is what made TestSprite valuable to me: it helped make verification a meaningful part of the development process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The experience reinforced something I want to carry into future projects:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Good software engineering isn't only about writing code that works. It's about understanding what the code must guarantee and collecting evidence that those guarantees hold.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Thank You, TestSprite!
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I want to express my appreciation to the TestSprite team for organizing Hackathon Season 4.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This hackathon gave me an opportunity to build a real project, explore software reliability problems, improve my engineering workflow, and learn more about automated testing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm grateful for the tools, the challenge, and the opportunity to improve.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Achieving &lt;strong&gt;97/97 passing TestSprite tests&lt;/strong&gt; on FlowGuard AI's final pull request was an exciting milestone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But more importantly, the experience helped reinforce a testing mindset that I want to continue developing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thank you, TestSprite, for being part of this journey!&lt;/p&gt;

