&lt;span class="na"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;job_redriven&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;jobId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;job&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;jobId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;retryCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;retryJob&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;retryCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;retry_failed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;instanceof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;channel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;nack&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;There are two operational choices worth calling out. A non-selected message is requeued, so this consumer should not be the only consumer of a busy DLQ: a batch process that lists messages and applies a filter may be a better fit at larger volumes. Also, &lt;code&gt;sendToQueue&lt;/code&gt; returning true only means the client accepted the write into its buffer; production code should use publisher confirms when the publish-before-ack boundary must survive a broker or connection failure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The handler still owns the hard part. Before expiring &lt;code&gt;reservation:42&lt;/code&gt;, it should verify that the reservation is pending and that its 15-minute deadline has passed. A second execution should observe the already-final state and produce no second side effect. Log &lt;code&gt;jobId&lt;/code&gt;, old retry count, new retry count, selection result, and terminal disposition. Without those fields, a later investigation sees a failure but not the retry path that produced it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Which queue fits this delivery decision?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The product choice changes the mechanics, but not the rule that a retry needs a bounded count and an idempotent handler. I would also judge an API platform by how quickly I can discover the exact request schema: a genuinely self-describing API with public discovery and runnable examples in multiple languages can remove SDK setup from this narrow integration task. The practical advantage is one REST API, no SDK to install, and one key for the backend capabilities this worker needs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Option&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Useful fit&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Important boundary&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;RabbitMQ&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Explicit exchanges, queues, and dead-letter routing; the example maps naturally to a DLQ consumer.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Redrive selection and retry metadata are application responsibilities unless you add your own operational tooling.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;BullMQ&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A Node.js-first queue backed by Redis, with job IDs and retry-oriented worker APIs.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Redis-backed job state and BullMQ semantics become part of the system; it is a different operational surface from a broker DLX.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Amazon SQS&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Managed queues with a dead-letter queue redrive model and visibility timeouts.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;AWS-specific configuration and IAM shape the workflow; inspecting and selecting individual messages is not the same as replaying a whole queue.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Temporal&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Durable workflows with explicit retry policies and long-running orchestration.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;It is a workflow engine, so it adds a larger programming and operating model than a focused queue redrive.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;An API platform with self-describing capabilities&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Useful when discovery matters: Infrai is one example with public capability discovery, request schemas, runnable examples, one REST API, and one key rather than an SDK to install.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The limitation is clear: it is not suitable for durable workflow orchestration; use Temporal for that. It still does not replace a database transaction or the worker's idempotency check.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I would choose BullMQ when the application is already committed to Redis and wants queue behavior close to its Node.js code. I would choose SQS when managed AWS operations and coarse-grained redrive are more valuable than broker-level control. RabbitMQ earns the choice when routing topology and explicit acknowledgements are central to the design. I’d choose Temporal when the expiry process becomes a multi-step workflow; a self-describing REST surface is the wrong tool if what you need is durable workflow state and joins.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the queue already exists behind a self-describing REST surface, the adapter can keep discovery and redrive separate. The two paths below are the verified DLQ list and redrive routes. The request body is loaded from an environment variable because the capability schema, rather than this article, should define the selection fields; hardcoding an invented body would make a copy-paste example misleading.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;apiKey&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;INFRAI_API_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;baseUrl&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;INFRAI_BASE_URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;queue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;INFRAI_QUEUE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;redriveBody&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;INFRAI_REDRIVE_BODY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;apiKey&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;baseUrl&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;redriveBody&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;INFRAI_API_KEY, INFRAI_BASE_URL, INFRAI_QUEUE, and INFRAI_REDRIVE_BODY are required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;GET&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;delayMs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;baseUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;Authorization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`Bearer &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;apiKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Content-Type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;application/json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Idempotency-Key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`reservation-redrive-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;429&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`DLQ request failed with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;retryAfter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;retry-after&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;resolve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;resolve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;isFinite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;retryAfter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;retryAfter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;delayMs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;delayMs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;unreachable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;failedJobs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/queue/dlq/list/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;encodeURIComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;GET&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dlq_listed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;queue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;failedJobs&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}));&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;redriveResult&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/queue/dlq/redrive/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;encodeURIComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;redriveBody&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dlq_redrive_requested&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;queue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;redriveResult&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This adapter is useful when the platform's discovery response is part of your deployment tooling: inspect the live schema, set the body for the selected job IDs, and keep the redrive operation auditable. It is not a workflow engine, and it is not a reason to skip worker idempotency.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That is the boundary.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This approach is not suitable for a long, stateful workflow with joins or durable replay history. For that job, choose Temporal or another workflow engine, use the scheduler only to enqueue work, and let a worker do the processing. A queue redrive can recover selected messages; it cannot infer the business state that makes a reservation expiry safe.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do not use this pattern as a substitute for a workflow engine. A fixed DLQ redrive is a useful recovery operation; it is not a DAG, a fan-out/join primitive, or a history-replay system. That distinction matters once expiry depends on several external steps.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What should you measure before automating redrive?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Start with three numbers: the count of failed jobs by reason, the age of the oldest DLQ message, and the number of attempts per &lt;code&gt;jobId&lt;/code&gt;. Add the count of messages moved to the terminal queue. These measurements tell you whether the problem is transient delivery failure, a deterministic bug, or an expired business assumption.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are hard boundaries to record in the runbook as well. A seven-day delayed-message limit and a 256 KB message limit are not interchangeable with durable event history. A standard queue's at-least-once delivery means the worker must stay idempotent. If a scheduler triggers the redrive, keep the trigger short and let a worker consume the jobs; a long-running expiry loop does not belong in a short cron execution.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The practical decision rule is simple: use the queue's native DLQ and redrive controls when they can select the intended messages, and put a small, auditable worker in front of them when they cannot. The worker should publish, confirm as far as the client and broker allow, acknowledge, and log. Three attempts is a reasonable starting boundary for this example, but the right value comes from the failure distribution, not from a magic constant.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


References
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RabbitMQ, “Dead Letter Exchanges”: &lt;a href="https://www.rabbitmq.com/docs/dlx" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://www.rabbitmq.com/docs/dlx&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BullMQ, “Retrying failing jobs”: &lt;a href="https://docs.bullmq.io/guide/retrying-failing-jobs" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://docs.bullmq.io/guide/retrying-failing-jobs&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Amazon Web Services, “Using Amazon SQS dead-letter queues”: &lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-dead-letter-queues.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-dead-letter-queues.html&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RabbitMQ, “Publisher Confirms”: &lt;a href="https://www.rabbitmq.com/docs/confirms" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://www.rabbitmq.com/docs/confirms&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


Quand une puce cérébrale rencontre la VR : mon retour d'expérience sur l'entraînement dichoptique pour l'amblyopie | Dev Blog
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;L'architecture repose sur un SoC neuromorphique basse consommation (≈15 mW) qui encode les signaux visuels en spikes asynchrones. Le pipeline VR utilise Unity 2022 LTS + XR Interaction Toolkit 2.3 ; le rendu stéréoscopique est géré par un single‑pass instanced shader, ce qui réduit le draw‑call overhead de ~38 % par rapport au multi‑pass classique. Côté logiciel, le module d'entraînement dichoptique implémente un algorithme de suppression interoculaire basé sur la différence de contraste (ΔC = 0,15 log units) et adapte la fréquence de présentation (30–120 Hz) via un contrôleur PID calibré sur la latence moyenne du casque (≈12 ms). Les benchmarks sur Quest 2 montrent une gaine de 90 FPS stable avec 2 ms de frame‑time GPU, laissant ~8 ms pour le traitement neuronal. L'API expose un endpoint gRPC &lt;code&gt;TrainSession/Start&lt;/code&gt; qui renvoie un flux de métriques JSON (latence, taux de spikes, score de suppression) pour un monitoring temps réel dans Grafana. Côté données, les sessions sont stockées en Parquet partitionnées par patient/jour, facilitant les requêtes analytiques avec DuckDB. Le trade‑off principal reste la calibration individuelle du seuil de suppression : un script Python (NumPy + SciPy) effectue une recherche dichotomique en ~0,4 s, acceptable en clinique. Prochaine étape : intégrer un modèle ONNX quantifié (INT8) pour prédire la progression du score en &amp;lt;5 ms, ouvrant la voie à un boucle fermée adaptative.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h1&gt;


Quand une puce cérébrale rencontre la VR : mon retour d'expérience sur l'entraînement dichoptique pour l'amblyopie | Dev Blog
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Je me souviens encore du soir où j'ai enfilé le casque dans mon petit bureau de Lyon, la lumière du crépuscule filtrant par la fenêtre. Mon fils de six ans, Léandro, luttait depuis des mois contre une amblyopie tenace ; les séances d'occlusion le laissaient frustré, les larmes aux yeux. Quand le neurologue m'a parlé d'un prototype associant une puce neuromorphique à la réalité virtuelle, j'ai hésité — trop technique, trop risqué. Pourtant, la promesse d'un entraînement dichoptique adaptatif, piloté par des spikes asynchrones, a réveillé ma curiosité d'ingénieur. La première session a duré dix minutes. Le casque a affiché deux images légèrement décalées, chacune modulée en contraste selon un algorithme PID que j'ai pu observer en temps réel sur mon tableau de bord Grafana. Léandro a ri quand les formes ont commencé à « danser » ; ses yeux, d'habitude figés, ont suivi le mouvement. Après trois semaines, le score de suppression interoculaire est passé de 0,12 à 0,04 log‑units, et le médecin a noté une amélioration de 2 lignes sur l'échelle de Snellen. Ce n'était pas de la magie, c'était des données, une latence de 12 ms, un cadre de 90 FPS stable, et surtout la joie de voir mon fils lire une bande‑dessinée sans plisser les yeux. Aujourd'hui, chaque nouvelle session ressemble à une petite victoire partagée entre code et cœur.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I wanted a place to count down to things – a trip, a birthday, a deadline – and to count &lt;em&gt;up&lt;/em&gt; from things, like the day I started a habit. Most countdown sites I tried were full of ads or wanted an account before I could type a date. So I built my own: CountMyDays. It's a solo side project, and this post is about how it's put together and a few things that bit me along the way.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The stack
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;React 19 + Vite + TypeScript&lt;/strong&gt; for the frontend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Supabase&lt;/strong&gt; for Postgres, magic-link auth and Realtime&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Vercel&lt;/strong&gt; for hosting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailwind for styling, and a service worker so it installs as a PWA and works offline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Nothing exotic. The interesting parts are in how data moves between "guest" and "signed in", and in how the timer stays accurate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Guest first, account later
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I didn't want a sign-up wall. When you open the app you can create countdowns immediately, and they're stored in &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; under a single key:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;STORAGE_KEY_LOCAL_COUNTDOWNS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;countmydays_local_milestones&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Pins and favourites live in their own small keys (&lt;code&gt;countmydays_pinned_ids&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;countmydays_favorite_ids&lt;/code&gt;) so they're cheap to toggle.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sign-in is passwordless: Supabase sends a magic link. The tricky bit is what happens to the guest data afterwards. I didn't want people to lose the countdowns they made before signing in, so after login the app maps the local items into rows for the &lt;code&gt;countdowns&lt;/code&gt; table and inserts them in one go:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;local&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Untitled Milestone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;trim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;slice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;120&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;target_date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target_date&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;targetDate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toISOString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;countdown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;is_pinned&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;is_pinned&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isPinned&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;is_favorite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;is_favorite&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isFavorite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;show_progress_bar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;show_progress_bar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;showProgressBar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;start_date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;start_date&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;startDate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;created_at&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;created_at&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;createdAt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toISOString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}));&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;supabase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;countdowns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;insert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;A few lessons from this:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Normalize on the way in.&lt;/strong&gt; Early versions stored camelCase (&lt;code&gt;targetDate&lt;/code&gt;), later ones snake_case (&lt;code&gt;target_date&lt;/code&gt;). The migration accepts both rather than pretending old data doesn't exist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Have a fallback for schema drift.&lt;/strong&gt; If the insert fails (for example an older database without the pin/favourite columns), it retries without those fields instead of failing the whole migration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Only clear local data after the insert succeeds.&lt;/strong&gt; The &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; keys are removed after Supabase confirms the rows, never before.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Security-wise, the browser only ever has the publishable key; what a user can read and write is enforced by Row Level Security policies in Postgres, so each row is tied to &lt;code&gt;user_id&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


A timer that doesn't drift
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The obvious approach is &lt;code&gt;setInterval(tick, 1000)&lt;/code&gt;. The problem is that intervals drift and can fire just &lt;em&gt;after&lt;/em&gt; a second boundary, so the display looks laggy next to a real clock.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead the timer is pure date math – every frame it computes the difference from &lt;code&gt;Date.now()&lt;/code&gt; – and a &lt;code&gt;requestAnimationFrame&lt;/code&gt; loop only calls &lt;code&gt;setState&lt;/code&gt; when the visible second actually changes:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tick&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;calculateLiveTime&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;targetDate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seconds&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;lastSecondRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;lastSecondRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seconds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTime&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;animId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;requestAnimationFrame&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Because the value is always derived from the clock, there's no accumulated error. Browsers pause &lt;code&gt;requestAnimationFrame&lt;/code&gt; in background tabs, so the hook listens for &lt;code&gt;visibilitychange&lt;/code&gt; and switches to a 500 ms interval while hidden, then back to rAF when the tab returns.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One small product decision lives in &lt;code&gt;calculateLiveTime&lt;/code&gt;: when a countdown passes zero, it doesn't just show "0". It flips to counting the elapsed time since the date. And "days since" trackers with a future start date count &lt;em&gt;down&lt;/em&gt; until they start. Same function, four cases.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Live shared links with Supabase Realtime
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every countdown can be shared via a public link. I wanted the shared page to update the moment the owner edits it – handy if you put a countdown on a TV and change the title from your phone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The shared view subscribes to one channel per countdown and listens to two things: Postgres changes on that single row, and broadcast events.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;channel&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;supabase&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;channel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`live_milestone_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;broadcast&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;milestone:live_stream&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* apply title / date changes instantly */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;broadcast&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;milestone:deleted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;onNavigate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;404&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;postgres_changes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;schema&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;public&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;countdowns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`id=eq.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* source of truth from the database */&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;subscribe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Why both? &lt;code&gt;postgres_changes&lt;/code&gt; is the reliable source of truth, but it only fires after the write lands. Broadcast lets the editor push changes straight to viewers with less delay. If the owner un-shares the countdown (&lt;code&gt;is_shared === false&lt;/code&gt;), viewers are sent to a 404 straight away.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On the sending side, I keep a small pool of joined channels in a &lt;code&gt;Map&lt;/code&gt; so repeated broadcasts don't re-subscribe each time. Channels are removed when the view unmounts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The Vercel SPA rewrite gotcha
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The app is a single-page app, so every route needs to serve the same HTML. The standard Vercel config is a rewrite that sends everything except the API to &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"rewrites"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"source"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/((?!api/).*)"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"destination"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/index.html"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That works – until you turn on &lt;code&gt;cleanUrls&lt;/code&gt;. While experimenting with adding static pages, I enabled &lt;code&gt;cleanUrls: true&lt;/code&gt;, and suddenly existing routes started returning 404. With &lt;code&gt;cleanUrls&lt;/code&gt;, Vercel serves &lt;code&gt;/index.html&lt;/code&gt; at &lt;code&gt;/&lt;/code&gt; and treats &lt;code&gt;.html&lt;/code&gt; paths differently, so a rewrite &lt;em&gt;to&lt;/em&gt; &lt;code&gt;/index.html&lt;/code&gt; no longer resolves the way you'd expect. The fix was to point the rewrite destination at &lt;code&gt;/&lt;/code&gt; instead:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"source"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/((?!api/).*)"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"destination"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The related SEO lesson: a catch-all rewrite also means &lt;em&gt;every&lt;/em&gt; unknown URL returns 200 with your app shell – a "soft 404" for search engines. I also had to add real &lt;code&gt;robots.txt&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;sitemap.xml&lt;/code&gt; files, because before that, those URLs simply returned the app's HTML.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I'd do differently
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Decide on one data shape on day one.&lt;/strong&gt; Supporting both camelCase and snake_case cost more code than it should.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Think about crawlers early.&lt;/strong&gt; A client-rendered SPA shows an empty &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;body&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; to anything that doesn't run JavaScript. Pre-rendering key pages is next on my list.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Keep the guest path.&lt;/strong&gt; Letting people try the app without an account was the best decision I made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you count down to anything – or count days since something – it's free and has no ads: &lt;a href="https://www.countmydays.to/?utm_source=devto" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;countmydays.to&lt;/a&gt;. Feedback on the code approach is very welcome in the comments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Last night I ran an SEO audit on Ilytics, the analytics tool I've been building, and it came back with 0 words on every page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I assumed the audit tool was broken. The site looked fine in my browser. So I fetched the homepage the way a crawler does, with curl and a Googlebot user agent, and counted the words in the HTML. There was exactly one: "Ilytics", from the page title. No headings, no text, no links to my other pages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix ended up being about twenty lines. It's an easy mistake to make in the App Router, so I'm writing it up.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The provider that wrapped everything
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My root layout wraps the whole app in an analytics provider, which is how most PostHog setups for Next.js look:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/layout.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PostHogProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PostHogProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Inside, the provider reads the URL so it can send a pageview whenever the path or query string changes. Because &lt;code&gt;useSearchParams()&lt;/code&gt; needs a Suspense boundary, I had wrapped it in one:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;PostHogInner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pathname&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;usePathname&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;searchParams&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useSearchParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...init, identify, pageview tracking...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PHProvider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;posthog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PHProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;PostHogProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PostHogInner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PostHogInner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Why that empties the page
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When a statically rendered page calls &lt;code&gt;useSearchParams()&lt;/code&gt;, Next.js can't know the query string at build time. So everything up to the nearest Suspense boundary gets rendered in the browser instead of on the server, and the server HTML contains the boundary's fallback.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My boundary wrapped &lt;code&gt;{children}&lt;/code&gt;, which in a root layout is the entire site. The fallback was &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt;. So every page was pre-rendered as nothing, and JavaScript filled it in after load.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Visitors never noticed because it happens in a fraction of a second. Crawlers that read the server HTML got an empty page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The fix is to shrink the boundary
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Only the part that reads the query string needs to wait for the browser. I moved pageview tracking into its own component, gave it its own Suspense boundary, and rendered &lt;code&gt;children&lt;/code&gt; outside of it:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;PageviewTracker&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pathname&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;usePathname&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;searchParams&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useSearchParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;ensurePostHog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;posthog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;capture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;$pageview&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;$current_url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;location&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;pathname&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;searchParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;PostHogProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// session and identify logic stays here, without useSearchParams&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PHProvider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;posthog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;fallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PageviewTracker&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PHProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The boundary now wraps a component that renders &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; anyway, so nothing is lost, and the actual pages render on the server again.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One thing broke along the way. React runs a child component's effects before its parent's, so the tracker started calling &lt;code&gt;capture()&lt;/code&gt; before the parent had called &lt;code&gt;posthog.init()&lt;/code&gt;. I moved the init into a small &lt;code&gt;ensurePostHog()&lt;/code&gt; function that both components call, with a flag so it only runs once.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Before and after
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I fetched the same pages as Googlebot before and after deploying. Visible words in the HTML:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home: 1 before, 375 after&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pricing: 0 before, 211 after&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FAQ: 0 before, 159 after&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Docs: 0 before, 138 after&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each page also went from zero to one H1, and from no internal links in the HTML to between 6 and 15.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How to check your own site
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Run this against any page and compare the number with what you see in the browser:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;curl &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-s&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-A&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Googlebot"&lt;/span&gt; https://your-site.com/ &lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;
| &lt;span class="nb"&gt;sed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-E&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'s/&amp;lt;script[^&amp;gt;]*&amp;gt;.*&amp;lt;\/script&amp;gt;//g; s/&amp;lt;[^&amp;gt;]+&amp;gt;/ /g'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;
| &lt;span class="nb"&gt;wc&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-w&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If it's close to zero, look for &lt;code&gt;useSearchParams()&lt;/code&gt; or other client-only hooks inside a Suspense boundary that sits high up in your layout.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Google does render JavaScript eventually, but it's slower and less reliable than reading HTML, and many other crawlers don't run JavaScript at all. I'd rather not depend on it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I'd check next time
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you add any tracking or auth provider to a Next.js layout, check where its Suspense boundary sits before you ship. The Next.js docs on &lt;a href="https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/functions/use-search-params" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;useSearchParams&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; explain the client-side rendering behavior in more detail.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It's a little embarrassing that the thing hiding my analytics product from search was an analytics provider. At least it made for a good debugging session.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Arsany&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;A small hook that stops a delayed callback from firing with yesterday's state — and keeps the timer's identity stable even when the callback changes on every render.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is a search box that looks right at a glance. Every keystroke updates the input and schedules a request. The previous timer is cleared, so only the last keystroke should fetch.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SearchBox&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setResults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;scheduleSearch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;timer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;clearTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;timer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;timer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/api/search?q=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;setResults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;scheduleSearch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The input is live. The data is frozen.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The URL is built from &lt;code&gt;query&lt;/code&gt; captured when the memoized function was created. That was the first render, where &lt;code&gt;query&lt;/code&gt; was &lt;code&gt;""&lt;/code&gt;. Type &lt;code&gt;react&lt;/code&gt;, wait 300 ms, and you get the results for an empty search. The component has a stale closure, and the empty dependency array is the cause.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The first fix is to add &lt;code&gt;query&lt;/code&gt; to the dependency array:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// before&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// after&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now every keystroke creates a new scheduler. The old timer is not cleared by the new one, because the &lt;code&gt;timer&lt;/code&gt; variable lives inside the old closure. A fast typist gets one pending timer per keystroke, each with its own query. If &lt;code&gt;scheduleSearch&lt;/code&gt; is passed to a child or used in an effect, the identity churn also causes re-subscriptions and defeats memoization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The second fix is to keep the scheduler in a ref and read the latest query from another ref:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;scheduleSearch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/api/search?q=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This works in a simple app, but writing a ref during render is not render-pure. React can start a render, let a higher-priority update interrupt it, and throw the first render away. The ref now holds a value from a render that never committed. In concurrent React, that is a correctness bug, not a style nit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The third fix is to put the callback in &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt; and accept the changing identity:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;scheduleSearch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/api/search?q=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;clearTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The timer is fresh, but the function is new on every keystroke. If an effect depends on it, the effect tears down and re-registers each time. If it is a prop to a memoized child, the child re-renders anyway. The debounce survives; the stable identity you needed does not.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You need one function to do two jobs: keep a stable identity for the timer and every effect that depends on it, yet read the newest state when the timer finally fires.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hook below splits those jobs. The scheduler is stable. The callback is read through a ref at fire time.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleCallback&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallbackRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;callback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;debounceTimerRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;clearTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;debounceTimerRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setValue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;(...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;args&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Parameters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;clearTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;debounceTimerRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;debounceTimerRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;args&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


The Mental Model
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Think of a mailbox with a fixed address and a replaceable letter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The mailbox is the function you get back. Its address never changes, so the timer, effects, and children always know where to send work. The letter inside is the callback. After every committed render, a new letter replaces the old one. When the timer finally rings, the carrier opens the box and reads whatever letter is there.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Identity:&lt;/strong&gt; the returned scheduler is the mailbox. It closes over a stable ref object, not over the callback value, so its identity survives callback changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Update timing:&lt;/strong&gt; the letter is replaced in a passive effect after commit. A render that never commits never becomes the letter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Read timing:&lt;/strong&gt; the wrapper reads &lt;code&gt;callbackRef.current&lt;/code&gt; when the timer fires, not when the timer is scheduled. That is the difference between fresh and stale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two consequences follow. An inline callback no longer resets the timer, because the scheduler's identity does not change. And a pending timer can call the newest callback with arguments from the call that scheduled it, so pass the exact value you want if that distinction matters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The mailbox never moves; only the letter inside changes.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How to Use It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hook has one helper. Put both files next to each other.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;src/
└── hooks/
├── use-callback-ref.ts
└── use-debounced-callback.ts
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;src/hooks/use-callback-ref.ts&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallbackRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;extends &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;args&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;never&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;callback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;callbackRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;callback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;callbackRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;callback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;((...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;args&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;callbackRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.(...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;args&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useCallbackRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;src/hooks/use-debounced-callback.ts&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useCallbackRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/hooks/use-callback-ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useDebouncedCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;extends &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;args&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;never&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;callback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleCallback&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallbackRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;callback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;debounceTimerRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;clearTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;debounceTimerRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setValue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;(...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;args&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Parameters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;clearTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;debounceTimerRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;debounceTimerRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;args&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Import it with your project's alias. Swap &lt;code&gt;@/&lt;/code&gt; for whatever alias you use.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useDebouncedCallback&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/hooks/use-debounced-callback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


Search as the user types
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useDebouncedCallback&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/hooks/use-debounced-callback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SearchBox&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setResults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useDebouncedCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/api/search?q=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;encodeURIComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setResults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;search&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The callback can be async, and the input updates immediately while the request waits. The scheduler stays stable across renders, so a new function identity does not restart the timer. Debouncing the request does not cancel requests already in flight; add &lt;code&gt;AbortController&lt;/code&gt; if out-of-order responses matter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Save a draft after the user pauses
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useDebouncedCallback&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/hooks/use-debounced-callback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;DraftEditor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;draft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setDraft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useDebouncedCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;nextDraft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Draft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/api/draft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;PUT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;nextDraft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;800&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;textarea&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;draft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;draft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setDraft&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;save&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Passing the next draft as an argument makes the delayed write carry the snapshot from the keystroke that scheduled it, while the callback itself can still see the latest render's state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Keep a listener subscribed once
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useDebouncedCallback&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/hooks/use-debounced-callback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Point&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useScrollReport&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;report&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useDebouncedCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;point&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Point&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/api/scroll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;point&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;250&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onScroll&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;report&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;scrollX&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;scrollY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;addEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;scroll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onScroll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;removeEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;scroll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onScroll&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;report&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The effect runs once because &lt;code&gt;report&lt;/code&gt; does not change when the callback body changes. That is the payoff: a stable dependency that still calls the latest code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Anti-pattern
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;❌ Do not call the debounced function during render.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useDebouncedCallback&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/hooks/use-debounced-callback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SearchBox&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useDebouncedCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/api/search?q=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Searching for &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This schedules a timer on every render, including renders caused by unrelated state, and it makes render impure. Call it from the event that actually happened.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


When to Use It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reach for this hook only when all three statements are true:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You need a delayed call from a rapid event, and only the final call's arguments should win.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The callback can change between renders because it closes over state or props, and it should use the newest committed version.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You need a stable function identity for a dependency array, a memoized child, or a long-lived subscription.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Situation&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Better tool&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;You need to cancel or flush the pending call&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A debounce utility with &lt;code&gt;cancel()&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;flush()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Every call matters and must run in order&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A queue or throttle&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;You are debouncing a value, not an event&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;useDeferredValue&lt;/code&gt;, or derive the value first&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The callback must run during server rendering or in Node&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A server-side scheduler with the correct timer type&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;You need to cancel in-flight network requests&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;AbortController&lt;/code&gt; in addition to debouncing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;You need the pending call to run on unmount&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Explicit cleanup or a library with &lt;code&gt;flush()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Smell test: if you cannot name the event that starts the timer and the render value that must stay fresh, you probably want a plain &lt;code&gt;setTimeout&lt;/code&gt; or a debounce library, not this hook.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How It Works Under the Hood
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The wrapper is the address.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;useCallbackRef&lt;/code&gt; returns a function created with &lt;code&gt;useMemo(..., [])&lt;/code&gt;. That function closes over the ref object, not over &lt;code&gt;callback&lt;/code&gt;. The inner call is &lt;code&gt;callbackRef.current?.(...args)&lt;/code&gt;, so the identity stays fixed while the value behind it changes. In current React the memoized wrapper is retained for the component's lifetime, though &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; is documented as a performance optimization rather than a semantic guarantee. &lt;code&gt;useDebouncedCallback&lt;/code&gt; then wraps the scheduler in &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;[handleCallback, delay]&lt;/code&gt;. Because &lt;code&gt;handleCallback&lt;/code&gt; is stable, changing the callback does not change &lt;code&gt;setValue&lt;/code&gt;. Changing &lt;code&gt;delay&lt;/code&gt; does, which is why the delay should be a constant or a memoized value.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The ref is updated after commit, not during render.&lt;/strong&gt; The helper uses &lt;code&gt;useEffect(() =&amp;gt; { callbackRef.current = callback; });&lt;/code&gt; with no dependency array. It runs after every committed render. This is deliberate. A render can be discarded before it commits; writing the callback ref during render would let a discarded render leak its callback into the live tree. The effect only exposes callbacks from committed renders. The read is deferred until fire time, which is why the timer never closes over the old callback.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The timer is a single slot.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;debounceTimerRef&lt;/code&gt; starts at &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt;. Every call clears the previous timeout and stores the new id. The unmount effect returns a cleanup that clears whatever id is current. Only the last call before the delay wins; earlier arguments are dropped. The cost is one timeout and one retained argument list per pending call. The cleanup happens on unmount, but not when &lt;code&gt;delay&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;callback&lt;/code&gt; changes. A pending timer keeps its original delay until it fires. There is no public &lt;code&gt;cancel&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;flush&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Effect ordering creates a narrow edge.&lt;/strong&gt; The callback ref is updated in a passive effect after commit. A timer that fires between commit and that effect would see the previous committed callback. For a normal debounce delay this window is effectively invisible, but it is not zero. In development, StrictMode runs effect setup, cleanup, and setup again on mount; the initial cleanup clears timer id &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt;, which is harmless unless you scheduled a timer from a layout effect in that gap.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The timer is browser code.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;window.setTimeout&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;window.clearTimeout&lt;/code&gt; are referenced only when the returned function is called or when cleanup runs. During server rendering, effects do not run and the returned function should not be called, so the component renders without touching &lt;code&gt;window&lt;/code&gt;. If you need the hook in Node or React Native, replace &lt;code&gt;window.setTimeout&lt;/code&gt; with the global timer and use &lt;code&gt;ReturnType&amp;lt;typeof setTimeout&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; for the ref type; do not call the returned function during SSR.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is the value at each phase. &lt;code&gt;S1&lt;/code&gt; is the scheduler identity; it stays the same as long as &lt;code&gt;delay&lt;/code&gt; does.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Phase&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;code&gt;callbackRef.current&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;code&gt;setValue&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Timer&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Initial render with callback A&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;S1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;none&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Commit and passive effect&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;S1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;none&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Discarded concurrent render with callback B&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;S1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;none&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;New committed render with callback C&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;S1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;none&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Passive effect after that commit&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;C&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;S1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;none&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;First &lt;code&gt;setValue("re")&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;C&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;S1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;T1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Next render with inline callback D&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;C&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;S1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;T1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Passive effect after that commit&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;D&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;S1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;T1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;T1 fires&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;D&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;S1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;fired&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The table shows the split: the callback slot moves, the scheduler does not. A discarded render never reaches the slot. A timer scheduled before a render can fire with the callback from before or after that render, depending on whether the passive effect has run.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt;, where your React version provides it, solves a related problem: an effect that needs the latest props or state without re-running. It is not a general-purpose debounce scheduler. Its function is meant to be called from effects, not passed to children or stored as an event handler, and it does not manage timer identity or cleanup. This hook solves a broader, older problem: a stable function you can hand to an event handler, a subscription, or a child, with the latest callback read when the timer fires.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Conclusion
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The tradeoff is small and deliberate: one stable scheduler, one mutable callback slot, one timer. You give up cancel, flush, and automatic rescheduling when the delay changes. In return, you get a function that can sit in dependency arrays without restarting the timer, while still calling the newest committed callback.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stable identity is not a frozen closure. The wrapper is stable; the callback is read at fire time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Update the callback after commit, never during render. A discarded render must not leak into the live tree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The pending timer is cleared on unmount, not on every change. Keep the delay stable and pass the exact arguments you want the delayed call to receive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use it when a debounced event handler must survive re-renders. Reach for a real debounce utility when you need &lt;code&gt;cancel&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;flush&lt;/code&gt;, or a timer that reschedules when the delay itself changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


1. Compute and Power Constraints
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mobile CPUs/GPUs are orders of magnitude slower than datacenter hardware. Running complex models continuously can overheat devices and deplete batteries. For example, on-device object detection may take tens of milliseconds per frame, far slower than server GPUs. One case study found that enabling GPU delegation reduced inference from ~28 ms to ~11 ms per image, illustrating how hardware accelerators help but only partially bridge the gap. In practice, heavy inference slows the UI and degrades UX. Developers must mitigate this by using quantized (INT8) or pruned models, leveraging mobile NN accelerators (NNAPI on Android, Metal on iOS), and limiting workload (e.g. reducing camera frame rate or downscaling images). Offloading to edge/ cloud (e.g. sending data to a server) avoids local load but adds network latency. In sum, AI features that demand high throughput or low latency (e.g. real-time video analysis) are often beyond pure on-device execution.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. Model Size and Architecture
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;State-of-the-art AI (LLMs, deep vision nets) contains hundreds of megabytes or more. Mobile storage is limited and models can’t be compressed by standard obfuscation. Large models inflate app size and may not fit in RAM. In one comparison, TensorFlow Lite’s library was ~20 MB smaller than PyTorch Mobile’s (minimized) binary, underscoring how framework choice affects footprint. Very large models simply won’t load on most devices. This means some AI tasks (e.g. on-device GPT-3) are infeasible. Mitigations include using compact models (MobileNet, DistilBERT) or on-device-specialized frameworks (LiteRT/TFLite, Core ML) that optimize size and performance. Techniques like pruning and quantization shrink models. Developers may also download models on demand or load from storage if necessary. Nonetheless, any feature requiring a “heavy” model forces trade-offs (e.g. degrade to simpler heuristic, or rely on cloud inference).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


3. Connectivity and Latency
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Complex AI often needs backend support. For large models or up-to-date data (e.g. user personalization), cloud APIs are used. But sending images or audio adds round-trip delays and requires bandwidth. One developer notes that even fast cloud inference suffers “massive overhead” serializing data, transmitting it, and encrypting it. Without a network (offline mode), these AI features fail outright. Conversely, on-device inference avoids connectivity needs and protects privacy, but then accuracy/complexity may suffer. A practical strategy is hybrid (“edge vs cloud”): run lightweight models locally and escalate harder tasks to the cloud if connected. Caching previous results, using quantized models for offline fallback, or pre-downloading data (e.g. language packs) can help. For non-real-time tasks, background syncing to the cloud when on Wi-Fi is another pattern. In short, AI features must gracefully degrade when offline or slow, for UX continuity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


4. Integration and Platform Constraints
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React Native does not natively run AI models in JavaScript at production speeds. Developers must integrate ML frameworks via native modules or JSI. As one example showed, implementing a TFLite image classifier in React Native required ~50 lines of Android (Kotlin) and iOS (Swift) code to preprocess frames and invoke the interpreter each time. This bridging adds development complexity and can be a maintenance burden. Cross-platform differences compound it: Android typically uses LiteRT/TFLite or PyTorch Mobile, while iOS favors Core ML or Metal-based inference. Code must handle both paths. Moreover, traditional RN bridge calls are asynchronous and could add latency; the new Hermes/JSI architecture (as used in react-native-vision-camera) helps by running code as native “worklets” to cut overhead. Still, any bug in the native side can crash the app. Developers mitigate integration pain by relying on well-maintained libraries (e.g. &lt;code&gt;react-native-tflite&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;react-native-vision-camera&lt;/code&gt; frame processors) and using architecture patterns that isolate ML logic. Employing Hermes or TurboModules also improves performance. But in general, RN’s JavaScript core cannot perform heavy AI by itself – native collaboration is required.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


5. Privacy and Security
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI features often process sensitive data (camera, microphone, personal info). Offloading to the cloud risks leaking user data unless encrypted – and even then, trust is a concern. On-device ML “avoids sending user-private data through the network”, which is great for privacy (e.g. facial analysis can stay local). However, embedding models on the device introduces intellectual property risk: attackers could extract or reverse-engineer your model. Studies warn that on-device ML models are targets for extraction attacks, exposing both the model and possibly training data. Developers should weigh these: for highly sensitive data (health, finance) on-device inference is safer for users, whereas for proprietary models cloud execution can better protect model IP. Mitigations include on-device encryption of model files, obfuscating code, or using secure enclaves/TrustZones. In either case, clear user consent and compliance (GDPR, etc.) are essential.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Custom Native Modules &amp;amp; Bridging (TurboModules)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React Native’s native modules require manual specification and binding code. For example, creating a &lt;strong&gt;TurboModule&lt;/strong&gt; involves writing a typed specification in TypeScript or Flow, running RN’s Codegen, and implementing native code on each platform. AI can generate a basic template, but it cannot reliably configure the native build environment or resolve platform-specific details. Official docs emphasize that a TurboModule is defined by “your specification, the native code you write, and the Codegen interfaces generated from your specification”.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// specs/NativeLocalStorage.ts (TypeScript spec for a TurboModule)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;TurboModule&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react-native&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;TurboModuleRegistry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react-native&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Spec&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;extends&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TurboModule&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;removeItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;clear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;():&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TurboModuleRegistry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;getEnforcing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Spec&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;NativeLocalStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Beyond codegen, many subtleties arise. For instance, Apple’s Swift language cannot call C++ (JSI) APIs directly, so bridging requires an Objective-C++ “glue” layer. React Native’s documentation specifically notes that iOS Swift modules need an adapter pattern with minimal Objective-C++ code to interoperate with RN’s C++ core. A human developer must correctly set up bridging headers, adjust symbol linkage, and handle issues (nil pointers, load-order quirks) that an AI model won’t foresee. In practice, you might define an Objective-C++ wrapper that calls Swift code, as in the React Native guide (e.g. creating a &lt;code&gt;NativeLocalStorage.mm&lt;/code&gt; that instantiates a Swift class). AI can’t test this on-device or catch linkage errors, so solving such integration bugs falls to developers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migration Tip:&lt;/strong&gt; When migrating to the new architecture, enable TurboModules and Fabric carefully. For Android, set &lt;code&gt;newArchEnabled=true&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;gradle.properties&lt;/code&gt;; for iOS, add &lt;code&gt;ENV['RCT_NEW_ARCH_ENABLED'] = '1'&lt;/code&gt; to the Podfile. Then rebuild and watch for crashes or missing modules (issues often show up in Xcode or Logcat).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Performance Profiling and Optimization
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React Native apps require manual performance tuning. The official docs state that RN “cannot determine the best optimization approach for you” in all cases – some problems need custom fixes. For example, large lists in a &lt;code&gt;FlatList&lt;/code&gt; must be configured with props like &lt;code&gt;windowSize&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;initialNumToRender&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;updateCellsBatchingPeriod&lt;/code&gt; to balance rendering and memory. The performance guide lists defaults (e.g. &lt;code&gt;windowSize = 21&lt;/code&gt;) and notes that increasing it can reduce blank areas but raise memory use. Adjusting these requires testing on target devices; AI cannot predict the optimal settings for your data. Likewise, stripping out debug code (e.g. &lt;code&gt;console.log&lt;/code&gt;) is often necessary. The docs even recommend using a Babel plugin to remove logs before production builds. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Moreover, RN runs two frame loops: the JS thread and the native UI thread. The docs explain that animations performed on the native thread (e.g. using &lt;code&gt;@react-navigation/native-stack&lt;/code&gt;) are smoother and not blocked by JS work. An AI model might suggest a JS-based animation, but a human developer can recognize when to switch to a native-driven animator or optimize JavaScript batching. As React Native notes, “native stack navigators… provide better performance… because the transition animations are executed on the native main UI thread”. Achieving 60 FPS often means profiling with device tools (Android Studio Profiler, Xcode Instruments), something only a human can operate. Even RN’s in-app Perf Monitor is just a guide – developers are advised to use native profilers for accurate metrics. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practical Example:&lt;/strong&gt; To tune a heavy list, try increasing &lt;code&gt;maxToRenderPerBatch&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;updateCellsBatchingPeriod&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;FlatList&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;windowSize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;21&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;initialNumToRender&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;maxToRenderPerBatch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;15&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;updateCellsBatchingPeriod&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then test on device to ensure scrolling remains smooth. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mitigation:&lt;/strong&gt; Profile on real hardware and iteratively tune. Use the React Profiler (in DevTools) to identify JS bottlenecks and native tools (CPU/GPU traces) for UI lags. Automating this reasoning is beyond current AI, so human analysis is key.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Native Debugging &amp;amp; Tooling
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Debugging React Native issues often requires human-driven, platform-specific tools. You can’t simply ask an AI to attach Xcode breakpoints or parse &lt;code&gt;adb logcat&lt;/code&gt; output in real time. Official docs explain that for native code, one typically “launches the app from Android Studio or Xcode and takes advantage of native debugging features (setting breakpoints, etc.)”. Likewise, checking platform logs uses CLI commands (&lt;code&gt;npx react-native log-android&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;log-ios&lt;/code&gt;) or IDE consoles. For example, native modules should log via Android’s &lt;code&gt;Log.d&lt;/code&gt; or iOS’s &lt;code&gt;NSLog&lt;/code&gt;, which developers then view in Logcat or Xcode. These live-run tasks – attaching to a process, stepping through C++ code, observing thread contention – cannot be done by a static AI model. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Moreover, diagnosing memory leaks or concurrency bugs requires monitoring. RN’s Dev Menu can show a simple perf overlay, but as docs caution, it’s only a guide and “native tooling under Android Studio and Xcode” is recommended for accurate analysis. Tools like Flipper or the Chrome debugger help inspect the JS side, but many timing issues or crashes stem from native threads or JSI. AI code suggestions won’t capture the actual runtime state. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Debugging Tip:&lt;/strong&gt; If your app freezes, attach the native debugger. In Android Studio use &lt;em&gt;Run → Attach debugger&lt;/em&gt;, and in Xcode use &lt;em&gt;Debug → Attach to Process&lt;/em&gt;. Then set breakpoints in Java/Kotlin or Objective-C++ code. This hands-on step-by-step inspection is something only a developer can perform. Rely on LogBox and console logs for JS errors, but remember that true native crashes (e.g. EXC_BAD_ACCESS) need native debugging, not just console output.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Example: remove console logs for production&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Babel config in .babelrc or babel.config.js&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;production&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;plugins&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;transform-remove-console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;(Configuring the build is another manual task; RN docs recommend removing logs for release builds to avoid JS thread bottlenecks.)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


New Architecture Migration &amp;amp; UI Quirks
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With React Native’s new architecture (Fabric and TurboModules), developers must adopt new patterns that AI can’t auto-insert. As the RN team notes, the new architecture allows synchronous layout measurement and concurrent rendering features. For example, instead of using the asynchronous &lt;code&gt;onLayout&lt;/code&gt; callback (which may cause visual jumps), developers can use &lt;code&gt;useLayoutEffect&lt;/code&gt; to synchronously measure views in Fabric, eliminating intermediate states. AI tools won’t automatically refactor your code to this model or understand the subtle timing benefits. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Similarly, enabling features like React 18 automatic batching requires opting into the new renderer. The documentation highlights that &lt;code&gt;useLayoutEffect&lt;/code&gt; in the new architecture performs measurements “in a single commit, avoiding the visual ‘jump’” seen in the legacy flow. Knowing when to use these new patterns versus old callbacks is something a seasoned developer decides during optimization. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Finally, the new architecture’s strict typing and codegen add hurdles. For instance, Swift-based AppDelegates cannot directly work with JSI C++ code, as noted earlier. Setting the &lt;code&gt;newArchEnabled&lt;/code&gt; flag requires touching multiple files (Gradle and Podfile edits) and understanding build nuances. If something goes wrong (e.g. a missing TurboModule causes startup to fail), a human must trace through native codegen logs. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migration Example:&lt;/strong&gt; Suppose you enabled Fabric (&lt;code&gt;newArchEnabled=true&lt;/code&gt;). You may find certain libraries need manual updates to their codegen specs. Check RN’s “What can I expect from enabling the New Architecture?” guide for version-specific notes. Always test on both iOS and Android after toggling the flag. Issues like symbols not found (&lt;code&gt;RCTCxxBridge&lt;/code&gt; errors) often require adjusting Podfile or rebuilding native modules. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Platform Quirks and Build Configuration
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each platform and OS version can introduce unique issues that AI can’t anticipate. For example, iOS’s new privacy permission dialogs or Android’s scoped storage changes often require platform-specific code or manifest edits. React Native’s native modules sometimes behave differently on device vs simulator. Only by testing on real hardware can a developer catch these quirks. The official docs do not enumerate every nuance (e.g. Bluetooth permissions, background task constraints), so developers rely on forums and GitHub issues for fixes. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Another example is build configuration: adjusting the Android &lt;code&gt;AndroidManifest.xml&lt;/code&gt;, editing the iOS &lt;code&gt;Info.plist&lt;/code&gt;, setting up push notification certificates, or configuring Google services JSON. These steps are manual and tightly coupled to the native environment. An AI model cannot set up your Xcode signing, Gradle keystores, or handle merge conflicts in &lt;code&gt;android/app/build.gradle&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer Tip:&lt;/strong&gt; Use the React Native &lt;a href="https://react-native-community.github.io/upgrade-helper/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Upgrade Helper&lt;/a&gt; to compare changes when bumping versions. For AndroidX or library incompatibilities, consult GitHub threads. AI-generated suggestions might miss these details. Document and script your platform-specific changes (e.g., CocoaPods post-install hooks or Gradle plugin settings) to avoid errors. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Today, I learned how React works with useState, how to define logic using functions, how to render UI elements, and how to target a particular element to display updated data.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React makes it easier to build interactive user interfaces by updating the UI whenever the state changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding useState in React
useState is a React Hook used to store and manage data inside a functional component. When the state changes, React automatically re-renders the component.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Syntax:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;const [value, setValue] = useState("");&lt;br&gt;
value – stores the current state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;setValue – updates the state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;useState("") – initializes the state with an empty string.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defining the Logic
After creating the state, we define a function to perform an action. For example, when a user clicks a button, a function can update the state.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;function greet() {&lt;br&gt;
setMessage("Hello, Welcome to React!");&lt;br&gt;
}&lt;br&gt;
Here, the greet() function contains the logic, and setMessage() updates the state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rendering the UI
In React, we use return() to render UI elements using JSX. JSX allows us to write HTML-like syntax inside JavaScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;return (&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
Click Me&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;{message}&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
);&lt;br&gt;
The button and heading are rendered on the page. When the button is clicked, the function updates the state, and React displays the new message.

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Targeting an Element
In React, we can display state data inside a specific JSX element using curly braces {}.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;{message}&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here, the &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt; element is the target where the message appears. When the state changes, React updates the displayed text automatically.&lt;/h1&gt;


&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete Example
import { useState } from "react";&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;function Greeting() {&lt;br&gt;
const [message, setMessage] = useState("");&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;function greet() {&lt;br&gt;
setMessage("Hello, Welcome to React!");&lt;br&gt;
}&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;return (&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
Greet Me&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;{message}&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
);&lt;br&gt;
}

&lt;p&gt;export default Greeting;&lt;br&gt;
How the Code Works&lt;br&gt;
State: useState("") creates an empty message.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Logic: The greet() function updates the message.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rendering: The return() statement displays the button and heading.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Targeting: The &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt; element displays the updated message.&lt;/h1&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Re-rendering: React updates the UI after the state changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conclusion&lt;br&gt;
Today, I learned the basic workflow of React: creating state with useState, defining logic using functions, rendering elements using JSX, and displaying updated values in a target element.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Understanding these concepts is an important step toward building interactive React applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As of October 27, 2026, this post sums up the official pages linked here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Someone on Reddit had a React app built with create-react-app and react-router. They put the build in an S3 bucket and served it through CloudFront. Moving around inside the app was fine. But if they pasted a deeper link like &lt;code&gt;/some-path&lt;/code&gt; into a new tab, or pressed refresh on that page, they got an XML page that said &lt;code&gt;AccessDenied&lt;/code&gt;. They asked how to send every path to &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt; while still letting the app see the real path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Plenty of teams hit this with single-page apps (SPAs) on AWS. The quick answer most people get is "add a custom error page." That answer works, but it has a side effect that often shows up weeks later. This post explains the root cause, why the quick answer can hurt, and a narrower fix with tested code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Root cause: two kinds of navigation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A React app with &lt;code&gt;BrowserRouter&lt;/code&gt; handles routes &lt;strong&gt;in the browser&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You open &lt;code&gt;https://example.com/&lt;/code&gt;. CloudFront returns &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt;, and the JavaScript loads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You click a link to &lt;code&gt;/dashboard&lt;/code&gt;. The router changes the address bar with the History API and draws the new screen. &lt;strong&gt;No request goes to CloudFront for &lt;code&gt;/dashboard&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You press refresh. Now the browser really does send &lt;code&gt;GET /dashboard&lt;/code&gt; to CloudFront.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CloudFront passes that request to the S3 origin, and S3 looks for an object with the key &lt;code&gt;dashboard&lt;/code&gt;. There isn't one. Your build only has &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt;, a few files under &lt;code&gt;assets/&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;static/&lt;/code&gt;, and some icons.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Why &lt;code&gt;403&lt;/code&gt; and not &lt;code&gt;404&lt;/code&gt;? With origin access control (OAC), CloudFront signs requests to a private bucket. AWS notes that if the bucket policy for OAC doesn't include &lt;code&gt;s3:ListBucket&lt;/code&gt;, S3 answers a missing key with &lt;code&gt;403&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;404&lt;/code&gt;. That is the &lt;code&gt;AccessDenied&lt;/code&gt; page from the thread. It isn't a permissions bug; it's a missing file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So the fix must do one thing: when the browser asks for an app route, CloudFront should serve &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt;, and the app should see the original URL. (The address bar keeps the original URL, so react-router still sees &lt;code&gt;/dashboard&lt;/code&gt;.)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The common fix, and its catch
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The usual advice, which also appears in AWS re:Post, is to add two custom error responses on the distribution:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;403 → &lt;code&gt;/index.html&lt;/code&gt;, response code 200&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;404 → &lt;code&gt;/index.html&lt;/code&gt;, response code 200&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It works for routes. Here is the catch: custom error responses are set on the &lt;strong&gt;distribution&lt;/strong&gt;, not on a cache behavior. In the CloudFront API, &lt;code&gt;CustomErrorResponses&lt;/code&gt; sits in &lt;code&gt;DistributionConfig&lt;/code&gt;, and there's no such field in &lt;code&gt;CacheBehavior&lt;/code&gt;. So the rule applies to every path the distribution serves.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That leads to three problems people hit later:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;API errors turn into HTML.&lt;/strong&gt; If &lt;code&gt;/api/*&lt;/code&gt; goes to an API origin through the same distribution, an API &lt;code&gt;404&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;403&lt;/code&gt; comes back as &lt;code&gt;200&lt;/code&gt; with your &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt;. The frontend's &lt;code&gt;fetch&lt;/code&gt; succeeds, &lt;code&gt;response.json()&lt;/code&gt; fails, and you see &lt;code&gt;Unexpected token '&amp;lt;'&lt;/code&gt; in the console instead of a clear 404.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Missing assets look like success.&lt;/strong&gt; After a deploy, an old tab may ask for &lt;code&gt;/assets/main.0a1b2c.js&lt;/code&gt;, which no longer exists. Instead of a 404, it gets &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt; with status &lt;code&gt;200&lt;/code&gt;. The browser then refuses to run HTML as a script, and the error points you in the wrong direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Real access problems disappear.&lt;/strong&gt; If a bucket policy breaks, every request still returns &lt;code&gt;200&lt;/code&gt;. Your error-rate graph stays flat while users see a blank page.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;None of this means the error-page fix is wrong. For a site with only static files and no API behind the same distribution, it's simple and fine. Once the distribution serves more than the SPA, a narrower fix is safer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


A narrower fix: rewrite only app routes
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of reacting to errors, decide &lt;strong&gt;before&lt;/strong&gt; the request reaches S3. A CloudFront Function on the &lt;strong&gt;viewer request&lt;/strong&gt; event can change &lt;code&gt;request.uri&lt;/code&gt;. You attach it only to the cache behavior that serves the static site, so the API behavior never runs it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The rule:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paths under &lt;code&gt;/api/&lt;/code&gt; (and &lt;code&gt;/.well-known/&lt;/code&gt;) pass through untouched.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If the final path segment has a dot (&lt;code&gt;main.0a1b2c.js&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;logo.svg&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;favicon.ico&lt;/code&gt;), treat it as a file and pass it through. A missing file still gets a real error.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Everything else is an app route. Rewrite it to &lt;code&gt;/index.html&lt;/code&gt;.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// CloudFront Function, runtime cloudfront-js-2.0, event: viewer-request.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Sends SPA routes to /index.html. Leaves real files and API calls alone.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PASS_THROUGH_PREFIXES&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/api/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/.well-known/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 1. API and other non-SPA paths go to their origin untouched.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;//    (Plain index loop: for...of is not on the runtime's supported list.)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PASS_THROUGH_PREFIXES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;++&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;startsWith&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;PASS_THROUGH_PREFIXES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 2. Anything whose last segment has a dot is a file (main.4f1c.js, logo.svg).&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;//    Keep it, so a missing file still returns a real error.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;lastSegment&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;substring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;lastIndexOf&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;lastSegment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;includes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 3. Everything else (/, /dashboard, /orders/42/) is a client-side route.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/index.html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;A few notes on the code:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It uses only features the CloudFront Functions JavaScript runtime 2.0 lists as supported: &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;let&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;String.prototype.startsWith()&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;String.prototype.includes()&lt;/code&gt;. The statement list in that runtime doesn't include &lt;code&gt;for...of&lt;/code&gt;, so the loop uses an index.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It changes only &lt;code&gt;request.uri&lt;/code&gt;. The browser's address bar still shows &lt;code&gt;/dashboard&lt;/code&gt;, so the router renders the right screen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;code&gt;/api/&lt;/code&gt; check is a safety net. The real protection is that the API has its own cache behavior with no function attached.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Wire it up with Terraform
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This config creates the function, attaches it to the default (site) behavior and gives &lt;code&gt;/api/*&lt;/code&gt; its own behavior. Note what's missing: there are no &lt;code&gt;custom_error_response&lt;/code&gt; blocks.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight hcl"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;terraform&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;required_providers&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;aws&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"hashicorp/aws"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;version&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"~&amp;gt; 6.0"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;variable&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"site_bucket_regional_domain"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;        &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Regional domain of the private S3 bucket, e.g. my-site.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;variable&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"api_domain"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;        &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Domain of the API origin, e.g. api.example.com"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;resource&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"aws_cloudfront_function"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"spa_rewrite"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"spa-rewrite"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;runtime&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"cloudfront-js-2.0"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;comment&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Send client-side routes to /index.html"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;publish&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;code&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;file&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"${path.module}/spa-rewrite.js"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;resource&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"aws_cloudfront_origin_access_control"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"site"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;                              &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"site-oac"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;origin_access_control_origin_type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"s3"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;signing_behavior&lt;/span&gt;                  &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"always"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;signing_protocol&lt;/span&gt;                  &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"sigv4"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;resource&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"aws_cloudfront_distribution"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"site"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;enabled&lt;/span&gt;             &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;default_root_object&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"index.html"&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;origin&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;origin_id&lt;/span&gt;                &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"site"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;domain_name&lt;/span&gt;              &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;site_bucket_regional_domain&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;origin_access_control_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;aws_cloudfront_origin_access_control&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;site&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;origin&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;origin_id&lt;/span&gt;   &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"api"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;domain_name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;api_domain&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;custom_origin_config&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;http_port&lt;/span&gt;              &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;80&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;https_port&lt;/span&gt;             &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;443&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;origin_protocol_policy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https-only"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;origin_ssl_protocols&lt;/span&gt;   &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"TLSv1.2"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Static site: the rewrite runs here only.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;default_cache_behavior&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target_origin_id&lt;/span&gt;       &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"site"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;viewer_protocol_policy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"redirect-to-https"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;allowed_methods&lt;/span&gt;        &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"GET"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"HEAD"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cached_methods&lt;/span&gt;         &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"GET"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"HEAD"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cache_policy_id&lt;/span&gt;        &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"658327ea-f89d-4fab-a63d-7e88639e58f6"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Managed-CachingOptimized&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;function_association&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event_type&lt;/span&gt;   &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"viewer-request"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;function_arn&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;aws_cloudfront_function&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;spa_rewrite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;arn&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# API: no rewrite, so a real 404 from the API stays a 404.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ordered_cache_behavior&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;path_pattern&lt;/span&gt;             &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/api/*"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target_origin_id&lt;/span&gt;         &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"api"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;viewer_protocol_policy&lt;/span&gt;   &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"https-only"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;allowed_methods&lt;/span&gt;          &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"GET"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"HEAD"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"OPTIONS"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"PUT"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"POST"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"PATCH"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"DELETE"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cached_methods&lt;/span&gt;           &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"GET"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"HEAD"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cache_policy_id&lt;/span&gt;          &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"4135ea2d-6df8-44a3-9df3-4b5a84be39ad"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Managed-CachingDisabled&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;origin_request_policy_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"b689b0a8-53d0-40ab-baf2-68738e2966ac"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Managed-AllViewerExceptHostHeader&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Note: no custom_error_response blocks. Those apply to the whole distribution.&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;restrictions&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;geo_restriction&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;restriction_type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"none"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;viewer_certificate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cloudfront_default_certificate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The three policy IDs are the AWS managed policies named in the comments. Each ID was matched against the AWS pages for managed cache policies and managed origin request policies. The S3 bucket policy that lets this OAC read the bucket is left out to keep the example short; the OAC page in the docs list below shows it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Trade-offs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No fix is free. Here is what this one costs and where it can bite:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Dots in route names.&lt;/strong&gt; A route like &lt;code&gt;/users/jane.doe&lt;/code&gt; looks like a file to this rule, so it won't be rewritten. Either keep dots out of route segments, or switch rule 2 to a short list of real file extensions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Unknown routes return 200.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;/no-such-page&lt;/code&gt; now gets &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt; with status &lt;code&gt;200&lt;/code&gt;. Your app must show its own "not found" screen. Search engines may treat that as a soft 404, so if SEO matters, render a not-found page and consider prerendering key routes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A function runs on every site request.&lt;/strong&gt; On pay-as-you-go pricing, CloudFront Functions are billed per invocation. Flat-rate plans count usage differently. Check the &lt;a href="https://aws.amazon.com/cloudfront/pricing/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;CloudFront pricing page&lt;/a&gt; against your traffic before you assume it's free.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Two places to change.&lt;/strong&gt; New top-level paths that should skip the rewrite (say &lt;code&gt;/auth/&lt;/code&gt;) need a new cache behavior, the prefix list in the function, or both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Why not the S3 website endpoint and its error document?&lt;/strong&gt; The OAC docs say a bucket set up as a website endpoint must be a custom origin, so you can't use OAC with it. You'd give up a private bucket to get the routing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If your distribution only serves the SPA, the two custom error responses are still a fair choice. Just know they act on every path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How to verify the fix
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Test the logic locally.&lt;/strong&gt; CloudFront Functions don't use &lt;code&gt;module.exports&lt;/code&gt;, so load the file the way a plain script runs and call &lt;code&gt;handler&lt;/code&gt; directly:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// test-spa-rewrite.mjs  (run: node test-spa-rewrite.mjs)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;readFileSync&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;node:fs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;vm&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;node:vm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;assert&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;node:assert/strict&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;vm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;runInNewContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;readFileSync&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;URL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;./spa-rewrite.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;utf8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;cases&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/index.html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/dashboard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/index.html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/orders/42/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/index.html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/settings/profile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/index.html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/index.html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/index.html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/assets/main.4f1c9a.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/assets/main.4f1c9a.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/assets/old.0000.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/assets/old.0000.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/favicon.ico&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/favicon.ico&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/api/orders/42&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/api/orders/42&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/.well-known/security.txt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/.well-known/security.txt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/v1.2/release-notes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/index.html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;expected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;cases&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;version&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;1.0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;eventType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;viewer-request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;GET&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;querystring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;cookies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;out&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;handler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;assert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;equal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;out&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;expected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; -&amp;gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;out&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;, expected &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;expected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`ok  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;padEnd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;28&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; -&amp;gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;out&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;uri&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cases&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; cases passed`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;On Node 20 all 11 cases pass. The last case matters: &lt;code&gt;/v1.2/release-notes&lt;/code&gt; has a dot in a folder name, but the rule only looks at the last segment, so it's still treated as a route. Node is more relaxed than the CloudFront runtime, so a local pass checks the logic, not runtime support. That's what the next step is for.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Check the Terraform.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;terraform fmt -check&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;terraform validate&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;terraform plan&lt;/code&gt; should show three resources and one &lt;code&gt;function_association&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;event_type = "viewer-request"&lt;/code&gt;. This config passed all three with Terraform v1.9.8 and the AWS provider v6.70.0.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Test in CloudFront before it goes live.&lt;/strong&gt; Save one request as &lt;code&gt;event.json&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"version"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"1.0"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"context"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"eventType"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"viewer-request"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"viewer"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"ip"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"198.51.100.10"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"request"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"method"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"GET"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"uri"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"/dashboard"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"querystring"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{},&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"headers"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{},&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"cookies"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then run it against the function's development stage:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;ETAG&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;aws cloudfront describe-function &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--name&lt;/span&gt; spa-rewrite &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--query&lt;/span&gt; ETag &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--output&lt;/span&gt; text&lt;span class="si"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
aws cloudfront test-function &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--name&lt;/span&gt; spa-rewrite &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--if-match&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$ETAG&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;--stage&lt;/span&gt; DEVELOPMENT &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--event-object&lt;/span&gt; fileb://event.json &lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;--query&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'TestResult.FunctionOutput'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--output&lt;/span&gt; text
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The output should show &lt;code&gt;"uri":"/index.html"&lt;/code&gt;. Change the URI to &lt;code&gt;/assets/main.0a1b2c.js&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;/api/x&lt;/code&gt; and check that they come back unchanged.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Check the live distribution.&lt;/strong&gt; After deployment finishes, with your real domain:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;curl &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--silent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--output&lt;/span&gt; /dev/null &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--write-out&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'%{http_code} %{content_type}\n'&lt;/span&gt; https://example.com/dashboard
&lt;span class="c"&gt;# expect: 200 text/html&lt;/span&gt;

curl &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--silent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--output&lt;/span&gt; /dev/null &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--write-out&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'%{http_code}\n'&lt;/span&gt; https://example.com/assets/does-not-exist.js
&lt;span class="c"&gt;# expect: 403 or 404, not 200&lt;/span&gt;

curl &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--silent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--output&lt;/span&gt; /dev/null &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--write-out&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'%{http_code} %{content_type}\n'&lt;/span&gt; https://example.com/api/does-not-exist
&lt;span class="c"&gt;# expect: whatever your API returns, e.g. 404 application/json, not 200 text/html&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If the third line comes back &lt;code&gt;200 text/html&lt;/code&gt;, a custom error response is still set on the distribution. Remove it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Before you ship
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[ ] No &lt;code&gt;CustomErrorResponses&lt;/code&gt; for 403/404 on a distribution that also serves an API&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[ ] The function is on the site behavior only, on &lt;code&gt;viewer-request&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[ ] &lt;code&gt;/api/*&lt;/code&gt; has its own behavior with no function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[ ] Route segments don't contain dots, or rule 2 uses an extension list&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[ ] The app shows its own not-found screen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[ ] Missing assets return 403 or 404, never 200&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you got here by searching for CloudSkill Consulting LLC software engineering, that's us. We wrote this fix for teams that serve a frontend and an API from one CloudFront distribution.&lt;/p&gt;

