&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudfront/latest/APIReference/API_DistributionConfig.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;CloudFront API: DistributionConfig&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudfront/latest/APIReference/API_CustomErrorResponse.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;CustomErrorResponse&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/GeneratingCustomErrorResponses.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Generate custom error responses&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/cloudfront-functions.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Customize at the edge with CloudFront Functions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/functions-javascript-runtime-20.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;JavaScript runtime 2.0 features for CloudFront Functions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/private-content-restricting-access-to-s3.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Restrict access to an Amazon S3 origin (OAC)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/using-managed-cache-policies.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Use managed cache policies&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/using-managed-origin-request-policies.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;managed origin request policies&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/cloudfront/test-function.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;AWS CLI: cloudfront test-function&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://registry.terraform.io/providers/hashicorp/aws/latest/docs/resources/cloudfront_function" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Terraform AWS provider: aws_cloudfront_function&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Spotted an AWS default or limit that changed since we wrote this? Drop a line to &lt;a href="mailto:info@cloudskillconsulting.com"&gt;info@cloudskillconsulting.com&lt;/a&gt; so the post stays accurate.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hey DEV Community! 👋&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I've been working on something for a while, and I wanted to finally share it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Meet &lt;strong&gt;Pimolu UI&lt;/strong&gt;, an open-source React component library I'm building with TypeScript.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The goal is pretty simple: create reusable, customizable UI components that look good, work well together, and make building interfaces a little easier.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why I started Pimolu UI
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are already plenty of great UI libraries out there, like shadcn/ui, HeroUI, Mantine, and others.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So why build another one?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I wanted to experiment with building my own design system, understand how component libraries work under the hood, and create something I could keep improving across different projects.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm not trying to reinvent everything. I'm trying to build something useful and learn along the way.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I'm working on
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A few areas I've been focusing on:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;React + TypeScript:&lt;/strong&gt; Reusable components with typed APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Customization:&lt;/strong&gt; Design tokens and CSS variables to make styling easier to adjust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Themes:&lt;/strong&gt; Consistent styling across components, including light and dark themes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Interactions:&lt;/strong&gt; Component states, transitions, and animations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Developer experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Making components straightforward to use and customize.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One thing I really want to get right is customization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I've used libraries where changing one small detail turns into fighting CSS overrides. I'm trying to avoid that with a token-based styling system.&lt;/p&gt;

